# TypeScript

- Prefer `interface` for object shapes; use `type` for unions/intersections
- Prefer named exports over default exports
- Avoid `any`; use `unknown` and narrow
- Type function params and public return values explicitly when inference is unclear
- Colocate types next to usage; shared types live in a dedicated module only when reused

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
interface UserCardProps {
  name: string
  role?: 'admin' | 'member'
}
```
